    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece of the lineup, boasting an elite 83.29 efficiency score. His matchup against Littell is highly favorable, driven by a 16% park factor boost and a significant dynamic platoon edge that, when combined with his strong BvP history, makes him the engine of our offensive projection. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.58) and **Josh Lowe** (68.96) offer high-ceiling value; while **Josh Lowe** suffers a minor penalty due to his lower batting order, his dynamic platoon advantage against Civale keeps his output well within the \"Strong\" start tier. We are also banking on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (68.72) to anchor the middle of the order, despite a slight regression in his dynamic platoon matchup against Rocker, as his base projection remains high enough to warrant a top-tier slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision today involved the final utility and outfield spots, ultimately resulting in **Coby Mayo** (61.64) being relegated to the bench. While **Coby Mayo** benefits from the same park and SP skill factors as **Gunnar Henderson**, his current projected efficiency fell just short of the starters, particularly **Wade Meckler** (57.26) and **Kyle Tucker** (64.46). **Kyle Tucker** remains a critical piece despite a sub-optimal batting order position, as his elite profile keeps him ahead of potential replacements. We continue to monitor the risk profiles for our outfielders; specifically, the efficiency scores for **Andy Pages** and **Josh Lowe** are slightly tempered by the defensive metrics of their opponents, which serve as a persistent drag on our SB upside. With no major weather concerns currently impacting our target venues, we are positioned to maximize our daily caps while prioritizing players with the highest potential for category-wide contribution.",
